+# Staging Alembic review — 2026-11-04
+
+> Release instruction update: apply only `0027_storage_lifecycle`; keep 0028
+> unapplied. Earlier audit results below are historical evidence. Current role,
+> metadata and approval requirements are in `staging-db-initialization-runbook.md`;
+> namespace setup is in `storage-namespace-initialization.md`. Older approval
+> hashes do not authorize this candidate. No hosted execution is authorized.
+
+> Execution update: [staging endpoint approval](staging-endpoint-approval.md) supersedes direct connection commands below. Use only its guarded entry points and verify-full TLS (or its explicitly approved, expiring isolated Render exception); the old artifact is preserved but does not authorize the new guard.
+
+Status: **conditional go for a fresh-database schema migration; Live preflight reported passed; HOLD for explicit execution approval and recovery-baseline acceptance. Local blockers fixed; staging verification still pending.** Only disposable local PostgreSQL migrations/tests were run for the follow-up fixes. No hosted database connections, deployments, or production changes were made. The reported committed provisioning and TLS login tests are accepted as user-supplied evidence, not independently rechecked database state.
+
+## Findings
+
+All 26 migration files were read. Local `.venv/bin/python -m alembic heads` and `history` confirm one unbroken base → 0001 → … → 0026 chain, no branch or missing parent. The head revision is **0026_application_runtime_grants**. An empty database must run the whole chain, not be stamped at 0020.
